Common Parameters (all tests)
==============================
  hmc_username      HMC user name
  hmc_pwd           HMC password
  manageSystem      HMC managed system (CEC) name
  slot_num          Space-separated vNIC slot numbers (range 3-2999, unused)
  vios_names        Space-separated VIOS names (one per backing device)
  sriov_adapters    Space-separated SR-IOV adapter location codes (DRC)
  sriov_ports       Space-separated port numbers (0 = first port on the adapter)
  bandwidth         Bandwidth entitlement % per vNIC port
  priority          Space-separated failover priorities (1=highest, 100=lowest, 50=default)
  auto_failover     1 to enable, 0 to disable (default: 1)
  device_ip         Space-separated IPs to assign to each vNIC
  netmasks          Space-separated netmasks (one per vNIC)
  peer_ip           Space-separated peer IPs used for ping validation
  peer_user         Peer LPAR login user
  peer_password     Peer LPAR login password
  mac_id            Space-separated MAC addresses for each vNIC
  count             Number of failover/disable-enable iterations (default: 1)
  num_of_dlpar      Number of DLPAR remove+add iterations (default: 1)
  host_public_ip    Public IP of the test host (used to copy eeh_tool to VIOS)
  host_password     Test host login password
  user_name         Test host login user

  Note: counts of slot_num, vios_names, sriov_adapters, sriov_ports, priority,
        mac_id, device_ip, netmasks, and peer_ip must all match.
        Failover tests and backing-device tests are skipped when len(slot_num) > 1.


Tests and YAML Files
====================

test_add / test_remove
  Add or remove one or more vNIC interfaces via HMC.
  YAML: any of the existing YAML files (single or multiple vNIC).
  Key params: all common parameters above.

test_backingdevadd / test_backingdevremove
  Add or remove secondary backing devices on an existing vNIC.
  Requires the vNIC to already be present (run test_add first).

test_disable_enable_dev
  Disable and re-enable a vNIC via HMC, verify link and ping survive.
  Uses: count for number of cycles.

test_hmcfailover
  Trigger HMC-initiated failover between backing devices, verify
  active device changes and connectivity is maintained.
  Uses: count, vios_ip, vios_username, vios_pwd (for pre-check).

test_clientfailover
  Trigger guest-initiated failover by writing to
  /sys/devices/vio/<id>/failover, verify connectivity after each flip.
  Uses: count.

test_vnic_auto_failover
  Swap priorities of active and backing devices, verify the backing
  device with priority=1 becomes active automatically.
  Requires >= 2 backing devices.

test_rmdev_viosfailover
  Remove the VIOS vNIC server and backing device via rmdev/mkdev on
  the VIOS, verify failover to the peer VIOS and connectivity recovery.
  Extra params: vios_ip, vios_username, vios_pwd.

test_vnic_dlpar
  Hot-remove and hot-add the vNIC via drmgr, verify IP and ping
  are restored after each cycle.
  Uses: num_of_dlpar.

test_vnic_hmc_dlpar
  Hot-remove and hot-add the vNIC via HMC chhwres, re-adding all
  backing devices after each add, verify connectivity each cycle.
  Uses: num_of_dlpar.

test_vnic_eeh
  Inject an EEH error on the backing device from the VIOS using
  eeh_tool_64, verify failover and connectivity recovery.
  Extra params: vios_ip, vios_username, vios_pwd, eeh_tool (path),
                host_public_ip, user_name, host_password,
                is_mlx_driver (true for Mellanox, false for lnc2).

test_sriov_vnic_same_port                    [NEW — vnic_sriov_same_port.yaml]
  Add one direct SR-IOV logical port AND one vNIC backed by the same
  physical adapter and port.  Verifies both interfaces come up and
  can ping their respective peers simultaneously, then removes both.
  Extra params (beyond common):
    sriov_mac_id      MAC for the SR-IOV direct logical port
    sriov_device_ip   IP to assign to the SR-IOV direct interface
    sriov_peer_ip     Peer IP for the SR-IOV ping check
  Run:
    avocado run network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_sriov_vnic_same_port \
              -m vnic_sriov_same_port.yaml

test_vnic_6x_single_card                     [NEW — vnic_6x_single_card.yaml]
  DLPAR-add 6 vNIC interfaces all backed by the same physical SR-IOV
  card.  Ports are distributed round-robin (0,1,0,1,0,1 for dual-port).
  All 6 interfaces are verified simultaneously with ping, then removed.
  Requires exactly 6 entries in slot_num; all sriov_adapters must be
  the same location code (repeated 6x).
  Run:
    avocado run network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_vnic_6x_single_card \
              -m vnic_6x_single_card.yaml

test_vnic_6x_multi_card                      [NEW — vnic_6x_multi_card.yaml]
  DLPAR-add 6 vNIC interfaces spread across at least 2 distinct SR-IOV
  cards.  All 6 interfaces are verified simultaneously with ping, then
  removed.  Requires exactly 6 entries in slot_num and at least 2
  distinct location codes in sriov_adapters.
  Run:
    avocado run network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_vnic_6x_multi_card \
              -m vnic_6x_multi_card.yaml

